{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777564051,"nonce":"VLd3nLBoxB4jwtVGLFkbOVS/UoA=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA9d-bA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/114","origin":"github"},"title":"Apply ignored_interfaces + diag noise reductions to BizzyBoat configs (2026-04-29 follow-up to #52)","message":"## Summary\n\nThe diagnostic-noise reduction mechanism from\n[`ros2_network_monitor#13`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/13)\nand the BizzyBoat annunciator/aggregator config from\n[`#52`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/52)\nboth shipped, but the boat-side launch is **not actually loading** the\n`ignored_interfaces` configuration — so the field-truth result is that\nseven distinct boat-side statuses are pinned at 100% WARN for an entire\ndeployment session.\n\nOperator-side does the right thing. Asymmetric — the same setup pattern\nwasn't applied to both sides when #52 closed.\n\n## Field evidence\n\nThe\n[2026-04-29 deployment](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/104)\nsurvey-session bag (`operator_2026-04-29T17.47.54`, 2h22m) recorded by\nthe salmon-side `/diagnostics` recorder (PR #109):\n\n| Status (boat-side) | total | WARN | %bad |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `mikrotik wifi.bizzy: interface/ether2` | 7511 | 7510 | 100% |\n| `mikrotik wifi.bizzy: interface/ether3` | 7511 | 7510 | 100% |\n| `mikrotik wifi.bizzy: interface/ether4` | 7511 | 7510 | 100% |\n| `mikrotik wifi.bizzy: interface/ether5` | 7510 | 7510 | 100% |\n| `teltonika router.bizzy: interface/mob1s2a1` | 7510 | 7509 | 100% |\n| `teltonika router.bizzy: mwan3/mob1s2a1` | 7509 | 7509 | 100% |\n| `teltonika router.bizzy: mwan3/wan1` | 7509 | 7509 | 100% |\n\nOperator-side equivalents (`mikrotik bizzy.wifi.op: …`,\n`teltonika router.op: …`) do not appear in the bad-row list — the\noperator-side mikrotik_monitor / teltonika_monitor are correctly using\ntheir `ignored_interfaces` configs.\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe `ignored_interfaces` lines exist in dedicated per-monitor YAMLs but\nthose YAMLs are never loaded on the boat side:\n\n```\nbizzyboat_project11/config/network_monitor_boat.yaml\n  mikrotik_monitor:\n    ros__parameters:\n      ignored_interfaces: ['ether2', 'ether3', 'ether4', 'ether5']\n\nbizzyboat_project11/config/teltonika_monitor_boat.yaml\n  teltonika_monitor:\n    ros__parameters:\n      ignored_interfaces: ['mob1s2a1', 'wan1']\n\nbizzyboat_project11/config/bizzyboat.yaml\n  /**/mikrotik_monitor:\n    ros__parameters:\n      host: 'wifi.bizzy.p11.lan'\n      poll_interval: 5.0\n      hardware_id: 'wifi.bizzy'\n      # NO ignored_interfaces\n\n  /**/teltonika_monitor:\n    ros__parameters:\n      host: 'router.bizzy'\n      poll_interval: 5.0\n      hardware_id: 'router.bizzy'\n      # NO ignored_interfaces\n```\n\n`bizzyboat_project11/launch/network_monitor_boat_launch.py` loads only\n`bizzyboat.yaml`:\n\n```python\nbizzyboat_config = PathJoinSubstitution([\n    FindPackageShare('bizzyboat_project11'),\n    'config',\n    'bizzyboat.yaml'\n])\nreturn LaunchDescription([\n    Node(package='mikrotik_monitor', ..., parameters=[bizzyboat_config], ...),\n    Node(package='teltonika_monitor', ..., parameters=[bizzyboat_config], ...),\n    ...\n])\n```\n\nvs. the operator-side launch\n(`network_monitor_operator_launch.py`) which loads the per-file YAMLs:\n\n```python\nparameters=[mikrotik_config]    # ← network_monitor_operator.yaml\nparameters=[teltonika_config]   # ← teltonika_monitor_operator.yaml\nparameters=[ping_config]        # ← ping_targets_operator.yaml\n```\n\nSo the boat-side `ignored_interfaces` configuration sits unloaded.\n\n## Tasks\n\n1. **Pick one source of truth** for the boat-side monitor configs and\n   remove the duplication. Two reasonable choices:\n   - **Fold the `ignored_interfaces` lines into `bizzyboat.yaml`'s\n     `/**/{mikrotik,teltonika}_monitor` blocks** and delete the\n     standalone `network_monitor_boat.yaml` /\n     `teltonika_monitor_boat.yaml`. Pros: matches the\n     \"everything in `bizzyboat.yaml`\" convention used elsewhere; one\n     file to edit. Cons: `bizzyboat.yaml` keeps growing.\n   - **Add the per-file YAMLs to the boat launch's `parameters=` list**\n     so both files merge at load time, mirroring the operator-side\n     pattern. Pros: symmetric with operator side; per-monitor configs\n     stay isolated. Cons: more files; ROS YAML merging is\n     order-sensitive (last file wins on key conflicts).\n\n   Either is fine — pick one and apply it consistently.\n\n2. **Verify post-fix** — redeploy, capture a fresh `/diagnostics` bag\n   (boat or salmon side), and confirm the seven statuses above are no\n   longer pinned at 100% WARN.\n\n3. **`mavros: Mount` constant WARN** — out of scope of this issue.\n   Track via:\n   - [`#87`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/87)\n     (mavros plugin allowlist) — if the mount plugin is dropped from\n     the load list, the diagnostic disappears entirely. Likely the\n     cleanest fix.\n   - Alternative: a separate mavros-config issue if the plugin needs\n     to stay loaded.\n\n4. **bencloud follow-up** — already removed from the annunciator.\n   Verify it's also removed from any other consumers:\n   - `bizzyboat_project11/config/ping_targets_boat.yaml` and\n     `ping_targets_operator.yaml`\n   - `bizzyboat_project11/config/diagnostics.yaml` (aggregator config)\n   - Any operator dashboards or alarm rules outside this repo\n\n## References\n\n- [`ros2_network_monitor#13`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/13)\n  — added the `ignored_interfaces` mechanism (closed)\n- [`ros2_network_monitor#16`](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/16)\n  — fixed the startup crash on `ignored_interfaces` (closed)\n- [`unh_echoboats_project11#52`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/52)\n  — created the boat-side annunciator/aggregator config (closed; this\n  issue is the field-truth follow-up)\n- [`unh_echoboats_project11#87`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/87)\n  — mavros plugin allowlist (related: `mavros: Mount` is a victim of\n  loading the mount plugin)\n- [`unh_echoboats_project11#104`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/104)\n  — the deployment that surfaced this; analysis in\n  `docs/logs/2026/2026-04-29_dev_logs.md` (timeline entry\n  2026-04-30T11:30-04:00, \"Salmon-side diagnostics analysis\").\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}